 AI transformation, service management, and cybersecurity offerings. Design, build, and maintain reusable enablers, accelerators, and reference architectures that reduce cost and time-to-value on federal client engagements. Recruit, mentor, and manage a multidisciplinary team of engineers, architects, and consultants, building a culture of innovation and continuous learning. Partner with business development and capture teams to shape technical solutions, proposals, and win strategies for federal opportunities. Cultivate strategic partnerships with cloud, SaaS, and AI technology vendors to bring emerging capabilities into FedTec's federal offerings. Serve as a trusted technical advisor to the firms technology leaders, translating mission needs into scalable, secure, AI-enabled solutions. \n Preferred candidate profile \n Minimum Requirements ( Mandatory ) \n 10 years experience in technology consulting, solution architecture, or IT capability/practice leadership. 4 years experience building and leading multidisciplinary engineering or consulting teams. Demonstrated experience architecting and delivering SaaS-based or AI-native solutions for enterprise or government clients. Working knowledge of federal cybersecurity and compliance frameworks (e.g., NIST RMF, FedRAMP, Zero Trust). Experience with hyperscaler cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, Google Cloud) and modern DevSecOps practices. Familiarity with agentic AI, large language models, and AI/ML platform engineering. Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field from a premier STEM institution. \n Preferred Qualifications ( Good to have ) \n Master's degree in Computer Science, Business Administration, or a related technical field from a premier STEM institution. Industry certifications such as AWS or Azure Solutions Architect, ITIL, or CISSP. Track record of standing up new practice areas or capability centers from the ground up.\n\nKey Skills: Artificial Intelligence,Solution Delivery,Practice Management,Cloud,Product Management,Product Delivery,Delivery Management,Product Development"},{"title":"Automation Test Engineer(Playwright)","company":"Experion","location":"Kochi","date_posted":"2026-09-09","url":"https://www.naukri.com/job-listings-automation-test-engineer-playwright-experion-kochi-thiruvananthapuram-6-to-11-years-090926009896","experience":"6-11 Yrs","is_walkin":false,"description":"Participate in the sprint planning / grooming sessions to understand the requirements and achieve good automation test coverage\n\nDuties and Responsibilities Following should be the responsibilities of a Senior Automation Tester: Work with the QA / BA team to convert the business requirements to automation cases\n\nExperience in Playwright tool\n\nKey Skills: Playwright,Automation Testing,Cypress,Software testing,Automation"},{"title":"Senior AI/ML Engineer","company":"Milestone Technologies","location":"Kochi","date_posted":"2026-09-11","url":"https://www.naukri.com/job-listings-senior-ai-ml-engineer-milestone-technologies-kochi-0-to-0-years-110926002886","experience":"0 Yrs","skills":[1,2,24,26,27],"is_walkin":false,"description":"6+ years AI engineering experience with strong Python fundamentals. Hands-on RAG pipeline and prompt-engineering experience. LLM application development experience. \n\nExperience building or validating golden Q&A datasets for grounding LLM systems \n\nDocument the upgrade path to fine-tuning (documentation only,not an implementation,in this phase). \n\nRequired skills & experience\n\nKey Skills: Orchestration,Tensorflow,Java,CSS,Integration,Artificial Intelligence,Semantic,Natural Language Processing"}]